  "lean": {
    "statement": "∀ {E : Type u_1}\n  {S : Type u_2} [inst : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_1 : InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [inst_2 : FiniteDimensional ℝ E]\n  [inst_3 : MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E] [inst_5 : MeasurableSpace S] (μ : MeasureTheory.Measure E)\n  [MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure μ] (b a : S → ℝ) (u : S → E),\n  Measurable b →\n    Measurable a →\n      Measurable u →\n        (∀ (s : S), 0 ≤ b s) →\n          (∀ (s : S), 0 < a s) →\n            ∃ T H B,\n              ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel T ∧\n                ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel H ∧\n                  ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel B ∧\n                    (∀ (s : S), T s = μ.tilted fun x => -(b s / 2) * ‖x - u s‖ ^ 2) ∧\n                      (∀ (s : S),\n                          H s =\n                            AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.GaussianSmoothing.gaussianSmoothing (T s)\n                              √(a s)) ∧\n                        (∀ (s : S) (y : E),\n                            B (s, y) =\n                              MeasureTheory.Measure.map (Prod.mk s) ((T s).tilted fun x => -‖x - y‖ ^ 2 / (2 * a s))) ∧\n                          (∀ (s : S) (y : E),\n                              B (s, y) =\n                                MeasureTheory.Measure.map (Prod.mk s)\n                                  (μ.tilted fun x =>\n                                    -((b s + (a s)⁻¹) / 2) * ‖x - (b s + (a s)⁻¹)⁻¹ • (b s • u s + (a s)⁻¹ • y)‖ ^ 2)) ∧\n                            ∀ (ν : MeasureTheory.Measure S),\n                              MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure ν → ⇑B ∘ₘ ν ⊗ₘ H = ν ⊗ₘ T",
    "statement_sha256": "ae058dcc7c38eadce546d9877be554162d5f3e63b79ad24ac23390f695be7150",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "Measure E is a countably additive measure. IsProbabilityMeasure means total mass one. Kernel X Y is a measurable assignment from X to measures on Y; IsMarkovKernel means every fiber has total mass one.",
      "mu.tilted(f) is the measure with density exp(f) divided by its integral against mu. No extra density or moment hypothesis is built into this notation.",
      "GaussianSmoothing.gaussianSmoothing(P,r) is the actual law of X+rZ under P times the centered identity-covariance standard Gaussian on E. The second parameter is a standard-deviation scale.",
      "Measure.map(f,P) is pushforward under f; Prod.mk s is x to (s,x). Norm and scalar multiplication are those of the real inner-product space.",
      "nu compProd H, written nu tensor_m H, is the joint law with first-coordinate law nu and conditional second-coordinate kernel H. B composed with M, written B circle_m M, is its bind. Equality means equality on all measurable sets of the product space. In this statement T,H are kernels from S to E and B is a kernel from S times E to S times E. S has just its specified measurable-space structure."
    ]
  },
